# Build & Typecheck

## Run the full gate before pushing

CI fails the branch on any of these, so run all of them locally first. A red
pipeline costs a full round trip; these take about a minute. From `desktop/`:

```bash
npm run typecheck
npm run lint
npm run dead-code:check
npm run test:unit
npm run service-contracts:check
```

The first four are exactly what `test:monorepo-gate` runs, in that order;
`service-contracts:check` is the separate `verify:service-contracts` job. Do not
report work as pushed or ready for review with any of them unrun.

`dead-code:check` is the one most often missed, because nothing else in the
local loop catches it — typecheck and lint both pass on an export that has no
importer. knip flags any exported value or type nothing imports, so a helper
exported out of habit fails the build. Fix it by:

- deleting it, if it is genuinely unused; or
- dropping the `export` when it is only referenced inside its own file — a type
  can annotate an exported function's signature without being exported itself
  (see `type-discipline.mdc`); or
- adding a justified entry to `desktop/dead-code-omissions.json`, only for a
  real false positive such as an export consumed by an external tool.

`npm run dead-code` (no `--check`) writes the same report without failing.

## Typecheck

- **Use `npm run typecheck`** to check types — not `npx tsc --noEmit` directly.
  The project has split tsconfig targets (`typecheck:node`, `typecheck:web`).
- **NEVER delete `.d.ts` files.** Some `.d.ts` files are authored sources
  (e.g. ambient type declarations in `src/`). Bulk-deleting them is destructive
  and irreversible. If `tsc` reports TS6305 ("Output file has not been built
  from source"), ignore those errors — they come from stale incremental output
  and do not affect the build.
- **Delete `*.tsbuildinfo` only** if incremental caches cause issues. These are
  safe to remove.
